sieve-filter-v2
; melody-gapfill-v1 for the notes3 family: after a leap, the next note steps back the other way.
; Rests are passed over. The state is the last note and what it owes (0 nothing, 1 a step down,
; 2 a step up).
; On a notes3 line the notes of one pitch, at every level and length, are one run of symbols,
; NOTE(p, 1, 1) to NOTE(p, LEVELS, LONGEST), and the rests another, REST(1) to REST(LONGEST).
id        melody-gapfill-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  After a leap, the next note steps back the other way.
param     leap     int     4   1  24  a move wider than this many semitones is a leap
param     step     int     2   1  12  the widest step that fills a leap, in semitones
param     resolve  choice  no  no,yes whether a melody may end on an unfilled leap

states    {1 + PITCHES * 3}
start     0
accept    0
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  accept  {1 + (p - 1) * 3}
  if {resolve == 0}
    accept  {1 + (p - 1) * 3 + 1} {1 + (p - 1) * 3 + 2}
  fi
done
t 0 @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} 0
for q 1 {PITCHES}
  t 0 @{NOTE(q, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(q, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {1 + (q - 1) * 3}
done
for p 1 {PITCHES}
  for owed 0 2
    t {1 + (p - 1) * 3 + owed} @{REST(1)}..@{REST(LONGEST)} {1 + (p - 1) * 3 + owed}
    for q 1 {PITCHES}
      if {owed == 0 || (owed == 1 && q < p && p - q <= step) || (owed == 2 && q > p && q - p <= step)}
        t {1 + (p - 1) * 3 + owed} @{NOTE(q, 1, 1)}..@{NOTE(q, LEVELS, LONGEST)} {1 + (q - 1) * 3 + (q - p > leap) + (p - q > leap) * 2}
      fi
    done
  done
done
end
